# Gemini Live API: Video Input & Interruption Handling

## Video Frame Transmission

Video frames are sent individually as images. The exact `sendRealtimeInput` shape for JavaScript is:

```javascript
session.sendRealtimeInput({
  video: {
    data: frame.toString('base64'),
    mimeType: 'image/jpeg'
  }
});
```

**Frame rate:** The documentation specifies a maximum of "1 frame per second."

## Media Resolution Configuration

You can constrain input media quality using the session config:

```javascript
const config = {
  responseModalities: [Modality.AUDIO],
  mediaResolution: MediaResolution.MEDIA_RESOLUTION_LOW,
};
```

## Interruption & Voice Activity Detection

### Detecting Interruption

When the user interrupts generation, the server signals this via:

```javascript
if (turn.serverContent && turn.serverContent.interrupted) {
  // Generation was cancelled
}
```

### Manual VAD Control

When automatic VAD is disabled, you manually bracket speech with:

```javascript
session.sendRealtimeInput({ activityStart: {} })
session.sendRealtimeInput({
  audio: {
    data: base64Audio,
    mimeType: "audio/pcm;rate=16000"
  }
});
session.sendRealtimeInput({ activityEnd: {} })
```

The documentation emphasizes using "at least **500ms**" silence threshold with manual VAD to avoid fragmenting natural pauses in speech.
[/external_agent_tool_result]

